# Story 68: Conversation History & Memory (45s)
# Hook: Recall any pane's conversation, and let old turns compact into summaries.
# Duration: 45s
# Source: story-068-conversation-history-memory.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 5

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
Recall any pane's conversation, and let old turns compact into summaries.

[00:03.0 --> 00:09.0]
Start rysh and split a second pane so we have two agents with separate conversations.

[00:09.0 --> 00:22.0]
From prompt mode, ask the agent to retrieve the other pane's conversation. The session_history tool reads any pane's turns.

[00:22.0 --> 00:36.0]
Drop into rysh mode to print this pane's history directly -- shell and prompt turns are all kept.

[00:36.0 --> 00:45.0]
As conversations grow, memory compaction folds old turns into compact MemoryEntry summaries -- context stays small and sharp.

